Good — `getReadTaskColumns` adds prewhere-required columns at read time, so the read itself doesn't lose prewhere columns. So the tree doesn't have the bug.

Therefore for slug 2, the best-faith minimal change is the regression test. I'll add a new test file pair replicating the PR's test additions (the query shape from the PR). Since 01710 doesn't exist, I'll create a new test `02455_projection_prewhere_missing_column.sql` / `.reference`. Content adapted from PR:

```sql
drop table if exists test;

create table test (name String, time Int64) engine MergeTree order by time;

insert into test values ('hello world', 1662336000241);

select count() from (select fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(time, 'UTC') time_fmt, name from test where time_fmt > '2022-09-05 00:00:00');

drop table test;
```
Reference: `1`.

The PR's original had it appended to 01710 which sets `set allow_experimental_projection_optimization = 1, max_rows_to_read = 3;` earlier in the session. To make the projection-optimization path active, include `settings allow_experimental_projection_optimization = 1` on the select. Expected result: 1 row? count() = 1. Yes reference "1".

